From: RetroArch-PI
Subject: [PATCH] new_dynarec arm64: encode the emit_andimm64 immediate outside assert()

emit_andimm64 called genimm(), which encodes the logical immediate into
armval, inside an assert(). The core is built with -DNDEBUG, so the call
was compiled out and the AND got whatever was left in armval on the
stack.

The only users are SDL and SDR, which clear the low address bits with
emit_andimm64(temp, ~3, temp) before writing the second word. The
garbage immediate turned that into, for example,
"and x1, x1, #0x100000001", and the following store went to 0x100000004:
SIGSEGV ("level 0 translation fault"). Conker's Bad Fur Day (USA) dies
this way 23-28 s in, at 100% speed until then.

Call genimm() first and assert on its result, as emit_testimm64 does.

---
--- a/mupen64plus-core/src/r4300/new_dynarec/arm64/assem_arm64.c
+++ b/mupen64plus-core/src/r4300/new_dynarec/arm64/assem_arm64.c
@@ -1902,8 +1902,9 @@
 {
   assert(rs!=29);
   assert(rt!=29);
-  u_int armval;
-  assert(genimm((uint64_t)imm,64,&armval));
+  u_int armval, ret;
+  ret=genimm((uint64_t)imm,64,&armval);
+  assert(ret);
   assem_debug("and %s,%s,#%d",regname64[rt],regname64[rs],imm);
   output_w32(0x92000000|armval<<10|rs<<5|rt);
 }
